---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, AUTHOR_DESC, CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_NAMES } from '../../data/site-config';
import { srcLink } from '../../lib/helpers';
import { KIT as K } from '../../lib/kit';
import { profilePageSchema, breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
const path = route('about', lang);
const title = 'Turkey bayram calendar publisher: who we are, data sources';
const description = 'The Turkish bayram, holiday and Ramadan timetable site is published by Radif Partners: independent, no donations. Data from the Diyanet and the law itself.';
const s = (k: string, t: string) => srcLink(k, lang, t);
const D = K.DOGRULAMA;
---
<PageLayout title={title} description={description} lang={lang} jsonLd={[profilePageSchema({ path, lang }), breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'About', path }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'About' }]}>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>About {SITE_NAMES[lang]}</h1>
    <p>{AUTHOR_DESC.en}</p>
    <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
    <p>"When is bayram?" is searched millions of times a year in Turkey. Most pages that answer give only the date, or put it in front of a holiday package, a sacrifice donation or a loan offer. The real questions are usually more concrete: how many days off will the feast give, is the eve a half day, is the holiday extended when it falls on a weekend, how many leave days buy how long a break, what time is the first iftar in my province? This site answers each of them on the first screen, with a computed result.</p>
    <h2>Who publishes it</h2>
    <p>The publisher is {AUTHOR_NAME}, a company that builds calculators from public rules and data. It is not a public body, part of the Diyanet, a law firm or a charity, has no link with any institution and uses no official emblem or logo. The site collects no donations, sells no sacrifice shares, travel or loans and carries no affiliate links. It asks visitors for no form, phone number or email address.</p>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
    <p>Feast, Ramadan, Laylat al-Qadr and holy-night dates come from the Diyanet's yearly lists of religious days, such as the <Fragment set:html={s('dg2027', '2027 list')} />. Which days are public holidays and how long they last is read from <Fragment set:html={s('k2429', 'Law 2429')} />. Holiday pay and annual leave come from <Fragment set:html={s('k4857', 'Labour Code 4857')} />, civil servants' leave from <Fragment set:html={s('k657', 'Law 657')} />. For administrative leave we check the <Fragment set:html={s('resmigazete', 'Official Gazette')} />; none has been published for 2027 and the site says so. Fasting times are computed with the Diyanet's parameters and checked against <Fragment set:html={s('namazvakitleri', 'its official prayer times')} /> over {D.karsilastirma.toLocaleString('en-GB')} prayer times, never more than a minute apart. The details are on the <a href={route('method', lang)}>method</a> page; corrections are handled as described in the <a href={route('editorial', lang)}>editorial policy</a>.</p>
    <h2>Your data</h2>
    <p>Every calculator runs in your browser. The province, year, leave days and wage you enter are neither sent nor stored. There is no account and no form. See the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <h2>What the site does not do</h2>
    <p>It does not approve leave, does not know your employment contract and gives no legal advice. It issues no religious rulings; on topics such as tarawih it reports what the cited source says. For worship, the Diyanet's official calendar prevails. School holidays are not covered.</p>
    <h2>Write to us</h2>
    <p><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> if a date, holiday length or prayer time looks wrong.</p>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
